abstract = {Matching domain services and application code has several use cases in software engineering, including software modernization, application integration, and documenting the application services. Establishing accurate matches between enterprise-specific domain models and application code is essential but challenging due to limited documentation and the complexity of large-scale systems. In this paper, we present a novel approach that leverages context-aware Generative AI (GenAI) to enable semantic matching between domain services and application classes. Our method enables a consistent representation of intent across artifacts, improving traceability between low-level implementations and domain-level abstractions. We validate our approach through a case study and experimental evaluation on an open-source, real-world enterprise system. The proposed method surpasses baseline average f1 score by +20%, with consistent gains in precision and service-level recall. © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).},
